  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Malaria - Guyana (01-Jan-2017-31-Dec-2019)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Guyana, Malaria, Ministry of Health of the Co-operative Republic of Guyana (MOH)This program has the following goals: To facilitate elimination of local P. falciparum transmission of by 2019 in low endemic regions.  To reduce overall malaria burden by at least 40% by 2019 particularly relative to 2014. The objectives of this program are: To optimize use of LLINs through IEC.  To reinforce coordination of all Malaria activities with Regional Health Departments and stakeholders.  To reinforce malaria diagnosis and treatment among high-risk and vulnerable populations.  To reinforce malaria surveillance, data management, and monitoring and evaluation (M&amp;E)</narrative>
  </description>
